── 2. THE CONVERSE — permission validator ALREADY INSTALLED ─────────────────
   (steady state: the case the 3,000,000 ceiling actually exists for)

   Method: toPermissionValidator accepts an explicit `permissionId`
   (toPermissionValidator.ts:71-73 short-circuits getPermissionId), so we can
   point a validator at a pId this account PROVABLY installed and let the SDK
   decide the mode by its own on-chain read. The signer contract still has to
   match — isEnabled compares permissionConfig(pId).signer against
   ECDSA_SIGNER_CONTRACT — so this is not a rubber stamp.

